  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Woof Haven Toulon is a fenced municipal field (6,000 m²), operated under a 6-year agreement with the City of Toulon, offered for private hire — not open access. On weekdays it works as a canine day-care (supervised care for sociable dogs); on weekends it is dedicated to activities and private hire (pool, cani-paddle, agility, mantrailing, cavage/den work). It's a valuable option for fearful, reactive or escape-prone dogs, who can burn off energy without running into other dogs or strangers.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Booking is online only, in advance. Rates are €18 per hour, €20 for half a day and €30 for a full day. Important correction: sessions actually welcome up to 6 dogs according to the official packages (park privatisation, day-care) — not 1 to 4 as previously stated. Activities supervised by a behaviourist/trainer are offered: canine playtime, agility, mantrailing, cavage (den work). Seasonal point of caution: a temporary closure was reported in February 2026 because of processionary caterpillars — worth keeping in mind in winter and spring.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: if your dog is fearful or reactive, a private session here can really make a difference — remember to book your slot online in advance.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Toulon and its surroundings are close by, handy for combining the session with other activities during the day.</p>
    </div>

